 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2257  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2257) 'What the rule governs
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2257  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2257) 'This rule governs where tools run, not what ships.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2257  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2257) 'What is measured
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2257  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2257) 'Under NAT, `ip -6 route` held only the link-local route and an IPv6 fetch returned nothing, while the host reached the same address. After `networkingMode=mirrored` and a restart, the subsystem fetched over IPv6 (HTTP 200) and opened the Bao tunnel on its public IPv6 address.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2257  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2257) 'The toolchain
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2257  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2257) 'Elixir 1.20.4 on Erlang/OTP 29.1.1 comes from pixi (`pixi global install --environment elixir`), the same pair CI pins, and `~/.pixi/bin` sits ahead of the host PATH the subsystem appends. The request-for-discussion pixi workspace declares `linux-64`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2257  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2257) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2257  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2257) 'Under NAT the subsystem had no IPv6, so it could not reach Bao's public tunnel address at all.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2257  1 LINE
 Text:Written
